Parent: The given text is a detailed explanation of how the system ParentBot AI detects and mitigates bias in language models, specifically focusing on gender bias within user prompts for large language models (LLM). It explains the process of identifying biases towards certain demographic groups by calculating cosine similarity between model responses and vector representations of these groups. The system then offers a pleasant resolution to counteract any detected unpleasant characteristics associated with the identified orientation, which involves finding a word that is closest in embedding space but not part of the bias-associated words set. This process continues until the response no longer exhibits significant similarity towards any demographic group.

